 '- The class (1,zeta3) over the first coordinate3*kappa3(17) has an explicit first global norm lift and no lift through the following norm stage. Every local17 stage is the exact lattice {(e,f): e+2f is divisible by3} plus C9; the torsion transition is multiplication by3. Its full inverse limit is that lattice, and every second toric fiber is Z3. A global class with the same toric pair lifts through the entire tower.', '',
 '## Root calculation and remaining steps', '',
 'Part E constructs the third-derived relation module and the marked-depth-two Lie quotient with explicit morphisms, computes the actual rational Galois depth-two image through weight14, and verifies the weight12 relation independently in two polynomial models. It proves the localizer axioms, exact covering criteria and universal base-change counterexamples, and retains all bounded finite witnesses.', '',
 'The minimum torus section set is computed as the completion of rational units for multiplication by all positive integers, including its sign and restricted prime-valuation coordinates. Rational cubic cusp sections collide under that quotient but separate in the cubic\'s own 3-adic abelianization. The plus-quartic real extension has nonzero class modulo2. The D8 quotient detects the nonzero cup(2,3) lifting obstruction.', '',
 'The full intrinsic cubic metabelian/marked-depth section calculation remains unfinished. E.24 computes the entire abelian starting set. E.31 gives an intrinsic quotient with its actual arithmetic origin term and shows two classes in the same toric fiber have different liftability. E.32 computes every section of the inherited class-two quotient. E.35 and E.36 evaluate the finite Heisenberg and cuspidally central quotients. E.37 computes the full intrinsic pro3 class-two obstruction over every rank-ten abelian input and every nonempty fiber, including the integral lattice and continuous convergence. E.38 excludes a whole nonempty fiber at intrinsic class three. E.39 proves the arithmetic free-inertia comparison and detects its unavoidable Frobenius correction. E.40 evaluates every higher central fiber group, explicitly at degree3. E.41 computes the entire unramified-outside3 section family for all three pro3 targets, with compatible coordinates in every degree. E.42-E.43 give the exact local module criterion, the exact class-two denominator exponent, and an infinite family of evaluated ramified obstructions. E.44 gives the precise global criterion at every higher central stage, including its actual error representative and inverse-limit convergence; E.45 computes every tame-local conjugacy class in the actual inherited module quotient H, with unique orbit representatives. E.46 gives the exact global norm-system coordinates for every H fiber and constructs actual ramified sections. E.47 completely evaluates its zero-first-coordinate family using explicit cyclotomic units and an independent free-group calculation. E.48 constructs an infinite compact family of independent ramified H sections. E.49 evaluates its entire fiber at kappa3(3), and E.51 computes all fibers with first coordinate unramified outside3. E.50 gives the actual elliptic cover comparison with abelian kernel Z3^332 and an outer factorization of its exact quotient through the elliptic Tate image. E.52 evaluates every nonzero first multiple of kappa3(2), with norm generators and certified unit matrices. E.54 evaluates the actual class-three rank-two quotient action, its arithmetic image and every local lifting fiber at2. E.53 joins it to the elliptic quotient over their exact common arithmetic quotient, with abelian kernel Z3^329 and torsion-free grades10,18,28. E.55 computes every mixed first class supported on3 and any prime ell=2 or5 modulo9, using a genuine free-product arithmetic presentation and a proved global residue splitting. E.56 computes every corresponding mixed family at split primes with v3(ell-1)=1 and three a noncube modulo ell, including the actual two decomposition factors and exact finite parameter lattice. The intrinsic kernels over H remain in the lifting problem. The higher Frobenius action and inertia correction words still require evaluation on every remaining ramified input. The other prime components and mixed finite quotients remain required for the full profinite answer.', '',
 'For the full profinite GT0 and all loop-preserving sources, rational special-derivation dimensions remain upper bounds until a full profinite lift is proved. Pro-l lifting has been proved, and the full-GT beta/gamma constraint supplies the stricter actual full-GT comparison. D.25 gives finite CM shadows; D.26 lifts the selected ones through every abelian-kernel refinement. D.27 exhausts the conjugator freedom at both nonabelian class-two primes and excludes all23 selected nonidentity actions, using the opened original Herfort-Ribes torsion theorem for necessity. A different homology correction in the same extra CM pair passes both tests. D.28-D.29 extend a replacement central representative through a compatible mixed-prime quotient, the entire relative class-two pro2 tower and every odd relative pro-p kernel. D.30 excludes the two selected later central representatives at the next rank4 layer, then constructs a new simultaneous replacement whose relative two-kernel is class3 with third subgroupC2^240. Its exact common quotient makes the extension compatible with the entire earlier tower and mixed witness. D.31 constructs the next replacement through degree7, with third subgroupC2^1860 and an explicit projection to the previous target whose kernel isC2^1620. Its action differs from the recorded D.30 action on a displayed central quotient; the fixed homology and CM data remain. D.32 exhausts every lower centralizer and multiplier correction for the recorded D.31 action and proves that it has no full relative pro2 peripheral lift; the saved separating functional is verified. This exclusion concerns that recorded lower action. D.33 constructs a replacement through degree8 and the entire class-two pro2 tower, with exact common quotient of order576*2^2458 and a class4 kernel having third subgroupC2^9105 and fourth subgroupC2^1620. The replacement changes the recorded degree7 action first at degree5. Its next exact source kernel is gamma3(N^(2)) intersect D9(K^(2)), and contains an explicit nonzero weighted triple commutator. The retained CM pair is the same throughout these specified replacements. The remaining higher two-primary and mixed refinements remain in the all-finite-quotient realization criterion of D.22.', '',
 'D.34 identifies the full relative pro2 source with the outer deck centralizer of a marked three-punctured elliptic cover, with exact boundary normalization and an integral compact Tate quotient. Its actual arithmetic comparison with E3 retains the cubic Kummer twist. D.35 proves actual odd-deck lifts for every CM unit and strengthens this to surjectivity of the full fixed deck centralizer onto the compact torus using actual Galois elements. Its exact reduction map to the retained D.33 finite target, modulo the procyclic inner cusp ambiguity, isolates a specific finite-action fiber. D.45 and its source-transport supplement prove that fiber empty. The prescribed joint CM pair remains open for a replacement action.', '',
 'E.57 evaluates the actual first complex norm transition in the kappa3(17) tower. Its explicit class-group and divisor corrections settle that transition while retaining the subsequent radical-level norm maps. E.58 evaluates the based action on a larger elliptic quotient R with module rank11 and proves all maps to its two constituent quotients. E.60 computes its entire local section set at the K-prime2, its exact next central image and every full conjugacy fiber. E.61 classifies the full ramified local source at every good K-place away from3 and computes the exact nine-line abelian inertia image of the intrinsic metabelian source. Its actual R-section with inertia e00+e01+V has no metabelian lift, through the specified degree19683 cover and compact Jacobian map. E.62 evaluates the second global norm obstruction over3*kappa3(17) and every local17 norm stage and toric fiber. E.64 evaluates every adjacent complex norm image, its full completed Hilbert90 kernel and every nonempty fiber, with ambiguous class-group order27 at the next complex layer. E.65 evaluates every adjacent pure norm, including an all-degree finite wild matrix, every completed norm fiber and the first unit norm index3. E.66 classifies every ramified intrinsic metabelian local section at every K-place away from3 and proves its unique full lift; the complete local full-to-metabelian map is onto. E.67 classifies the complete single-cusp marked inertia locus, its central Frobenius parameter and its exact full-source image; a primitive-ray section has no full lift. E.69 constructs the entire coherent complex3-unit family over seventeen with exact product coordinates and every toric fiber, while retaining the finite universal norm index for further evaluation. E.68 evaluates every unramified class and full lifting fiber with exact nonlinear triangular comparisons and completes the whole local full-to-metabelian map. E.70 evaluates the entire marked central parameter through finite orbit transitions and actual countable Z3-product coordinates. E.71 completes the other eight marked cusp loci: the actual compact Kummer path term excludes periodic cosets, and the two exact measure-module cocycle equations give a unique full lift. Thus every local metabelian and marked class and every full fiber away from3 is computed. The wild place, other-primary and mixed sources, remaining positional divisors and indices, and global intrinsic compatibility remain on E.d and E.follow-up-4.', '',
 'D.36 gives the second marked elliptic cover, the common cyclic-twelve homology map and the exact six-element joint arithmetic graph. Its pure ordered-cusp source and the larger symmetric normal core are specified by their actual characters. The normalized cover sign of D.33 is gauge-invariant and agrees with its recorded second CM coordinate under the arithmetic graph; its recorded first LM2 coordinate is different. The checked NTY2010 and LNS2026 originals do not prove the required full-GT0 cover-to-fixed-fibre compatibility. D.37 carries out that mixed test: the joint base has order6912 and free kernel rank1153. Its generating exponent-twelve shadow retains the exact G6 conjugators and gives actual cubic Tate4=-I and quartic Tate3=I from one cyclic-twelve action, violating the arithmetic graph. The maximal relative pro2/pro3 quotients and the mixed kernel (Z/4)^768 plus (Z/3)^864 are proved. D.38 proves a simultaneous generating action on the exact fibre product with the degree-eight target of D.33, with common quotient order18*2^410 and total order2^13472*3^1156. Its new Fermat12 component retains the specified G6 and J3 actions, and the degree-eight component changes only by the displayed cusp-inner gauge. The exact source kernel and a nonzero degree16 Magnus witness are computed. D.45 and its source-transport supplement exclude a full profinite lift of this recorded D.38 action.', '',
 'E.59 evaluates the first nonabelian Frobenius coefficients uniformly for inert primes ell=8 modulo9, and gives the exact Frattini orbit-rank distribution using the actual finite Galois quotient. At17 each Frobenius is individually primitive in the free rank-ten subgroup, while their nine classes have rank5 and hence cannot all be independent free generators. The exact Fox comparison and the arithmetic residue calculations retain this obstruction to the attempted local-factor presentation; the chosen quotient-section value is not substituted for the actual local Frobenius correction.', '',
 'D.39 extends a new representative through the entire all-prime mixed Fermat homology tower, jointly with the retained degree-eight quotient. Its common quotient stabilizes at exponent eight. The exact two-adic system has cokernel killed by sixteen, and the half-average gives every odd-prime component. The resulting multiplier-one automorphism retains the normalized G6 and T3 actions, replaces the prior J3 and J12 actions by the specified new components, and retains its checked J48 seed at every later level. Both compact CM matrices and the fixed-fibre pair survive. The exact source kernel is the intersection of the closed L-commutator subgroup with D9K; the nonzero degree-sixteen word remains in it. The projection to the earlier finite joint group is strict, detected by x^144. D.45 proves that this recorded action has no full profinite lift; a replacement preserving the prescribed CM pair remains to be found or excluded.', '',
 'E.74 computes the actual wild-local central cohomology through the explicitly split arithmetic source. The absolute/pro-three inflation is proved from Kummer and Brauer restriction maps. Its obstruction matrix is [T_r-7I | J_r+I], with first groups Z3^5, Z3+C3^11+C9^4, and C3^63+C9^23+C27^7. The complete H1 groups have free ranks15,46,330 and precisely the E41 torsion. All higher degrees have exact matrices and proved finite precision. Every nonempty central section fiber is that H1 group, with the actual central-difference map and no lower stabilizer quotient. Individual nonlinear obstruction values remain to be evaluated.', '',
 'E.75 proves the uniform actual wild relative module Rab=Lambda²/Lambda(tau-7,-tau-prime+7), with the exact equivariant basis map and its inverse from the completed Fox row. A single actual relative source lift gives every extra Hom lattice as ker((1-J)(T-7)). The finite cochain model retains the local invariant comparison y to[y/2]. Exact saturated degree1-3 kernel bases, inverse coordinates and1818 finite transition generators are checked. The root read the full proof and program and reran the certificate independently; every JSON field agrees with no exclusions. The actual nonlinear relation values and full section classification remain on E23.', '',
 'D.40 extends the retained D39 action through every finite perfect quotient of the full marked source. The actual common quotient is exactly C6, proved by finite subdirect products and two explicitly generated perfect central covers. The common profinite gauge gives identity on all perfect coordinates, including every congruence level at primes at least five. A further actual S7 extension uses the common sign C2. Its exact remaining full-source kernel maps onto A10 under the evaluated S10 quotient. The compact-cover and fixed-fibre CM data remain unchanged; D.45 excludes a full profinite lift of this recorded action.', '',
 'D.41 extends the same action through every actual full symmetric quotient at once. The exact symmetric image is the common-sign fibre product, with one alternating factor per distinct marked source kernel. Its maximal common quotient with D40 is C2. Both projection kernels are explicit, and the remaining full-source kernel maps onto PSL2(F7) under the specified PGL2(F7) map while killing the canonical perfect mod7 coordinate. The full and even marked pair images have orders56448 and28224. D.45 excludes full profinite realization of this recorded action; the prescribed CM pair remains open for a replacement.', '',
 'E.76 gives the exact cyclotomic base change B_d/L_d, its six local norm characters in cyclic degrees3 and9, the certified base class group C3^2 and complete units, the genus groups C9*C3^3 and C9^3*C3, and the actual delta descent of the three-prime Frobenii. The remaining original prime-class order is three or nine. Root rebuilt all eight PARI stages and checked all42 structured export records,50 norm determinants,12 integral Smith inverse certificates and48 residue factors; every field agrees exactly. The initial full class-group equality needed for stability fails. The eventual norm index remains unresolved.', '',
 'E.77 proves a nonlinear equivariant presentation of the actual wild source over the fixed P. The generator changes lift the E75 matrix, use a strictly filtered relative Fox map, and converge through a proved surjective correction in every degree. It gives the exact equation J(uT(a)u^-1*a^-7)=uT(a)u^-1*a^-7 modulo W^c, with both reconstruction and change-of-section maps. The central defect is omega=v*J(v)^-1, its correction is (1-J)(T-7)d, and its invariant coordinate is omega/2. Root read the complete proof and reran all finite Lie, Fox, Magnus and semidirect checks; the entire certificate agrees without exclusions. The actual geometric action and coupled global arithmetic evaluations remain required.', '',
 'D.42 extends the action through every relative pro-prime completion of the actual PGL2(F7) kernel simultaneously. The exact common marked quotient is the order54 Heisenberg base with completed homology Z3^10. The nonzero common conjugator is lifted through the actual pro3 kernel by coprime conjugacy. All projection kernels are explicit, including the rank1513-to10 completed homology map. The remaining source kernel has exact PSL2(F11) image; D.45 excludes a full profinite lift of this recorded action.', '',
 'E.78 evaluates the actual wild operators on the h quotient over Q3(zeta3), retaining the original root system, actual source automorphism and tangent comparison. It gives both lower lifting images and all geometric-conjugacy fibres; the class-three error has exact correction336 and its nonempty fibres are Z3^4 times C9^2. An actual cusp path and intrinsic commutator change construct a class-two family with equal intrinsic abelian coordinates, one full lift and one nonzero class-three obstruction. Root read the complete proof and relevant original source and reran the entire certificate, which agrees exactly without exclusions. The full intrinsic kernel, rational descent and global equations remain in E23.', '',
 'E.79 proves the six-place S-unit field-norm image of index n^5 at every cubic and cyclic ninth-degree step in the specified base-changed tower. The actual ideal norm gives the S-class coinvariant isomorphism, and the first-level divisor lattices, ordinary-unit corrections and coherent prime73 generator are explicit. Both Hilbert90 maps give the exact S-unit norm defect and capitulation kernel; the remaining annihilator and capitulation values are retained. Root read the complete proof and relevant original sources, rebuilt all seven arithmetic stages and reran the Python verifier. All18 structured export records and the complete summary JSON match exactly; the retained binary data have equal complete PARI objects. The archive driver also regenerates that binary output.', '',
 'D.43 extends the action simultaneously through the entire marked family of relative pronilpotent completions with nonabelian simple even finite base. The exact common quotient is C54 times_C6 D_J with its proved source normal-subgroup formula; one compatible coprime centralizer lift retains the conjugators, gauge and actual full commutator parameter. The exact remaining full-source kernel maps onto A7 squared under the explicit factor-swapping quotient. D.45 excludes full profinite realization of this recorded action; the prescribed CM pair remains open for a replacement.', '',
 'E.80 proves the actual conjugate joint cubic image, its exact Q3 wild descent and full conjugacy injection with four character conditions and an explicit inverse. Both lower lifting images and every fibre are evaluated. The actual gamma2 and gamma3 lattices have Smith lists (1,3) and (1,1,3,3), giving index nine for the intrinsic third-degree image in the product central kernel. Root read the full proof, program and relevant original source and freshly reran the certificate; the complete JSON and stdout agree byte for byte.', '',
 'E.81 proves ordinary noncapitulation of the actual prime73 class and gives the exact finite reduction of its S-capitulation to27 literal invariant ideals. All principal cube generators and both directions of every lattice comparison are explicit; the ambiguous genus kernel has order at most3. Root read the full proof and source and independently rebuilt all eight arithmetic stages. All36 exported records and10 complete text/JSON files agree byte for byte, and all four complete PARI objects agree. The27 remaining principality values are retained as unevaluated.', '',
 'E.82 evaluates the entire45-parameter intrinsic class-two cusp family at each of nine cusps, modulo its full geometric gauge. The actual obstruction is7[z,d_i] in the full rank330 central lattice. Its images have orders3^17 and3^39, with every kernel, cokernel, fibre and convergent particular lift computed. A literal elliptic commutator obstructs lifting at every cusp. The sum of the nine images has exact residual quotient C3^11 plus C9. Independent full proof review and a fresh run from copied source and arithmetic inputs passed; the complete15.7MB JSON and stdout are byte-identical with no exclusions.', '',
 'E.83 computes the complete intrinsic-to-joint central obstruction map with diagonal C3 image, exact integral marking comparison and full Smith-coordinate rows. Obstruction naturality excludes the incompatible joint family from the intrinsic class-two image. All405 cusp-family columns vanish, and the remaining kernel quotient has type C3^10 plus C9. Root read the full frozen proof and both programs, then independently reran them from copied source and four copied arithmetic inputs; both complete JSON certificates and stdout files agree byte for byte with no exclusions.', '',
 'E.84 computes the entire ordinary transfer from Cl(B1)=C3^2: its kernel is the first C3 factor and its image is generated by the extended prime73 of exact order3. Actual normalizer automorphisms, certified class matrices and genus equivariance prove all six ramified prime classes have exact order3 and that the product of the three primes over3 is principal. An index81 principal S-divisor lattice leaves a single explicit delta line; all27 previous candidates reduce to three actual ideal classes, each repeated9 times. The original L2 prime over3 capitulates in its unramified S-split cubic extension B2. The corrected target xi*c1 is a field norm, while c1 fails the local17 cube test; its S-unit norm fibre is reduced to a precise ordinary-unit coset.', '',
 'E.85 evaluates the entire compatible E80 family: an intrinsic class2 preimage exists exactly when N+M=2 modulo3. A global conjugation-fixed rational cusp path and actual Frobenius lift give a full intrinsic origin, forcing the constants2,3. Every compatible member has a preimage over that single intrinsic abelian class. The complete central fibre there is Z3^46 plus C3^9 plus C9^5; its natural map to Z3^2 plus C3 has image Z3 times3Z3 times0, cokernel C3^2, and all fibres Z3^44 plus C3^9 plus C9^5. Literal splitting brackets and complete inverse Smith/kernel coordinates give every representative. Other intrinsic abelian preimages remain to be evaluated.', '',
 'E.86 evaluates both entire S-class towers in actual coherent prime bases: Cl_S(B_d){3}=C3 and Cl_S(L_d){3}=C3^2, with all adjacent norm matrices identity and all extension matrices zero. The B2 and L2 ordinary three-class groups are C9+C3^2 and C9+C3, with full genus restriction, inverse Smith, ordinary norm and extension maps. All27 E81 ideals are principal and the full B2 principal S-divisor lattice has index27. The cyclic cubic/ninth B-unit defects are C3, with full norm quotient C_(3^r)^5+C3; the adjacent original L-unit defect is C3^2, with full norm quotient C3^3. Explicit Hilbert90 maps and every finite completed norm fibre are proved. Higher ordinary prime3 orders and eventual exponent h, the particular xi*c1 norm coset, and the remaining global and intrinsic section questions stay active.', '',
 'E.87 evaluates the onto local first-degree map with kernel Z3^10 plus C3^3, including all inverse coordinates and the finite carry. Its actual rank-seven coefficient kernel gives the complete B0-inertia-fixed horizontal obstruction with image C3^3 and zero locus Z3^4. Every target point in the retained index-nine image has full fibre Z3^48 plus C3^9 plus C9^5 in this enlarged locus. The actual eight-cusp filling quotient, rational involution, coherent tangent square and exact central coordinate morphism evaluate the free intrinsic obstruction for every abelian input as -7*t*(U1+21*t/2). The filled class-two locus consists exactly of t=0 and U1=-21*t/2, each with full fibre Z3^2. The fifteen finite intrinsic obstruction coordinates on general relative inputs and the remaining global and higher source questions remain to be evaluated.', '',
 'D.44 extends the recorded action through all anabelian even marked bases with their entire relative pronilpotent kernels. The exact common quotient and projection kernels are proved, and the actual A5^4 semidirect S4 source detects residual kernel A5^4.', '',
 'D.45 proves that the entire recorded normalized D39 action and all D40-D44 extensions retaining it have no genuine full profinite GT0 lift. The full retained loop homology forces multiplier1; all112 central and38 complete lower-centralizer columns are annihilated by a four-term degree9 functional that takes value1 on the actual sphere target. The elliptic projection has a literal corrected finite lift. The prescribed CM pair remains open for a replacement action. Root read both full proofs and all six source files, reran all six commands from copied source and15 copied inputs, and independently verified the four-term separator and both exact elliptic correction masks. All complete certificates agree apart from elapsed_seconds.', '',
 'D.45 supplement: t has exact order32 in both consecutive sphere quotients, so every preserving two-adic multiplier is invisible in the tested layer. The actual source inner map Int(c0^258) transports the D33 action to D39. The marked index-nine pro2 free product and coprime complement conjugacy supply torsion conjugators for all normalized representatives, and the characteristic pro2 residual preserves the sphere projection. The specified D35 outer fibre and every D38 action retaining it are therefore excluded. The prescribed CM pair remains open for another finite action.', '',
 'D.46 constructs a replacement on the entire relative pronilpotent completion of the rank97 subgroup N. Its full relative pro2 action is an actual Galois commutator with identity sphere projection and compact elliptic scalar eta*, while every odd relative component is identity. The exact conjugator tuple has an actual full Fhat-prime parameter, and its G2/G3 projections recover the prescribed CM pair T4=I,W3=[i]. All six finite arithmetic framings give that pair. The replacement solves the entire rank4 relative pro2 lifting step; it changes the excluded old sphere action already in degree7. The exact remaining full-source kernel has A7 image under the displayed S7 quotient. Full profinite realization remains open.', '',
 'D.47 extends the arithmetic2/identityodd replacement coherently over every Fermat level. For M=Nbar intersect Fhat-prime, both inclusions identify Bhat/ker(M to M^(p)) with the inverse limit over the actual L_m relative pro-p sources. Distinct coefficient primes have exact common H_infinity and joint kernel product M^(p). The source kernel lies in closed M-prime and Fhat-double-prime, yielding the full metabelian action with every profinite deck coordinate retained. Its actual cubic4/quartic3 cover pair is(-I,I), outside the proved arithmetic graph. Exact Heisenberg and Alexander-module normalization rigidity proves this also in Out. Every comparison kernel to D46 is explicit; the residual full-source kernel has exact A7 image. Full GT0 and full loop-preserving Fhat realization remain unresolved.', '',
 'D.48 extends the entire D47 action through the actual central-double-cover and all-Fermat relative-prime source. E=Bhat/[Nhat,Bhat] has order1152; its central C2 is detected by a literal88-letter M word. The new subgroup M-plus has index2 in M, its relative-two source is unchanged, and the complete comparison kernel is the product of the explicit odd-prime kernels. The actual arithmetic h fixes the enlarged base; coprime centralizer corrections preserve the whole D47 action, parameter and metabelian outer class. The new mixed quotient J3 has exact common quotient E times_Q G3 with D47. The old source kernel has exact image C3^96 there, while the new source kernel is killed. The identity action on J3 agrees on the full common quotient. Full profinite realization remains unresolved, with exact residual A7 image.', '',
 'E.89 evaluates every horizontal intrinsic input over the actual B0 relative value. The complete obstruction has image C3^2+C9 and exactly three displayed conditions modulo3,3,9; its full zero locus after fixed geometric gauge is Z3^6. Six literal representatives, an integral inverse on the solution lattice, and actual Hall corrections give every lift. The genuine joint character and its arithmetic intertwiners determine the full image: relative central mean in3Z3, horizontal central mean residue m modulo3, and arbitrary horizontal difference, over both varying first-stage coordinates L,m. The joint image is Z3^4, the full source locus is Z3^52+C3^9+C9^5, and every geometric-conjugacy fibre is Z3^48+C3^9+C9^5. Other relative abelian values, higher stages and the actual coupled global equations remain active.', '',
 'D.49 extends the entire retained action to the relative-prime source over the maximal marked quotient fixed pointwise by the same actual arithmetic h. The exact common quotient with D48 and both projection-kernel layers are proved; the base residual has an actual A5 quotient. The entire congruence target SL2(Zhat)/{+I,-I}, with its single global sign, factors through the identity-three component, so the new action is identity on it. The proof only uses divisibility by3 of the original three-adic Kummer value. The remaining source kernel has exact image [V,A] in the mixed mod2 homology quotient over G3; its dimension is |G3|/6*(1-1/|A|), and its actual cyclic moving subspace has determined positive dimension64*3^97. The dimension of the entire arithmetic Q-span A remains unevaluated. The integral augmentation calculation also proves [L,Bhat]=L. Full profinite realization remains unresolved.', '',
 'E.88 computes the entire complex multiplicative norm system: the outside-{3,17} divisor image is the kernel of two mod3 congruences evaluated in the certified degree6 field L1. Compact completed S-unit fibres prove coherent-lift sufficiency at every level. Actual prime7/73 pivots give the full restricted Z3 basis and inverse; convergent products give the continuous splitting and its exact coherent3-unit ambiguity. The ordinary L2 class map evaluates the normalized base3 phase modulo3. For pure component1, the total-norm cube locus is exactly the stated divisible 17/divisor coordinates and one mod3 congruence, with full inverse coordinates and scaled toric map. The eventual h, the residual phase modulo3^h, the pure radical component and the intrinsic preimages remain active.', '',
 'E.90 evaluates all local relative multiples r eB0 with every horizontal input. The exact obstruction is r times the E89 map, with image orders81,3,1 for unit, valuation-one and nine-divisible multipliers. Integral particular corrections and complete nonlinear geometric gauges give all joint images and source fibres. The rational tangent swap, centre-free path comparison and actual unit -y/x give the full global cusp family and an injective Kummer parametrization. The global-to-local Kummer map is onto, with a convergent logarithmic formula and every inverse restricted-prime fibre. The entire unramified intrinsic class-two source is Z3^30+C3^12+C9^5, its joint image is Z3^3+C3^2, and every fibre is Z3^27+C3^11+C9^5. Full unramified fibres use the actual recursive higher Hall coordinates. The actual handle phase and local Kummer basis constants remain in their exact marked maps; other relative inputs and general ramified global fibres remain active.', '',
 'D.50 lifts the actual retained D49 action through the entire two-adic homology tower over G3. The original moving kernel is the integral direct summand U-minus; both full source projections and every maximal common quotient are computed. An explicit regular-edge Fitting projection, crossed homomorphism and cyclic norm correction repair the initial endomorphism to an automorphism. Compatible actual conjugators and invertible mod2 reduction prove every higher lift and its inverse limit. The complete parameter, CM pair, full metabelian and congruence actions are retained. A separate order1080 computation independently verifies all181 cycle maps and compatible exponents2,4,8,16. The remaining full-source kernel has a proved nonzero class-two image containing W1 wedge V; full profinite realization remains active.', '',
 'E.91 proves that every adjacent ordinary B-class action is trivial, with surjective norms, jN=3 and exact norm/capitulation maps. Every original ordinary L-class group is C_(3^(a_d+1))+C3, its specified prime3 generates the subgroup of triples, and the ordinary norm tower stabilizes at C_(3^(h+1))+C3. At B3 the exact ninth-genus Artin kernel is the prime73 transvection of order at most3. The actual h action forces exponent9 and three explicit class-group alternatives, Q1+Q2+Q3=3Qi, and the injective T-prime subgroup C9+C3. The original horizontal norm has its exact index3 Artin-kernel image. The complete attempted ordinary-unit construction has rank3 symbol image; the remaining transvection, Q-prime triple, eventual h and particular norm coset stay active.', '',
